  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant signal (RNA-only 0.485 vs image-only 0.208), and the multimodal setup (config_021, 0.527) adds only ~4 points over RNA alone. All three completed experiments used pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder, so we have no information on whether a learned nonlinear representation (scvi_n200) could improve the primary signal. Question: config_008 is identical to config_021 except for swapping pca_n2000 → scvi_n200, cleanly isolating the RNA encoder effect while holding image encoder (resnet50), profile (single), aggregation (None), and fusion (concat) constant. Why this is the best next experiment: Since RNA drives most of the performance, improving its representation has the highest expected impact. A single-variable comparison to config_021 gives a direct, interpretable readout on whether a deep generative encoder helps over linear PCA, reducing uncertainty about the most consequential design axis before investing in more complex multiprofile/aggregation/fusion variations."
}

